<section class="product-category-landing">
    <div class="container">
        <p class="product-category-landing__eyebrow">DYNAMICS 365 CRM</p>
        <h1>On-Premises Dynamics CRM</h1>
        <p class="product-category-landing__intro">iFOX provides Dynamics 365 on-premises consulting and Dynamics CRM on-premises support to help organizations maintain secure, reliable customer operations while planning practical improvements.</p>
        <div class="product-category-landing__grid">
            <a href="/dynamics-365-crm-services/CRM%20Consulting"><strong>CRM Consulting</strong><span>Assess your on-premises CRM environment and align improvements with business needs.</span></a>
            <a href="/dynamics-365-crm-services/Implementation"><strong>CRM Implementation</strong><span>Plan and configure an on-premises CRM environment around your processes and users.</span></a>
            <a href="/dynamics-365-crm-services/Customization"><strong>CRM Customization</strong><span>Adapt CRM processes, forms, workflows, and configuration to business requirements.</span></a>
            <a href="/dynamics-365-crm-services/Support"><strong>CRM Support</strong><span>Maintain and troubleshoot your on-premises CRM environment as needs evolve.</span></a>
        </div>
        <div class="product-category-landing__content">
            <h2>Dynamics 365 On-Premises Consulting and Implementation</h2>
            <p>iFOX helps organizations assess, implement, configure, and improve on-premises CRM environments around their business processes. Our <a href="/dynamics-365-crm-services/CRM%20Consulting">CRM consulting</a> and <a href="/dynamics-365-crm-services/Implementation">on-premises CRM implementation</a> approach starts with understanding users, data, security needs, integrations, and operational priorities. We then review the existing environment or implementation plan, configure appropriate CRM components, validate key processes, and prepare practical documentation for users and administrators.</p>
            <p>This work can help teams organize customer information, improve process consistency, reduce avoidable manual effort, and make CRM operations easier to manage. We focus on changes that support the organization’s day-to-day requirements without assuming that every environment needs the same configuration or development approach.</p>

            <h2>On-Premises CRM Maintenance, Administration, and Support</h2>
            <p>For existing environments, iFOX provides <a href="/dynamics-365-crm-services/Support">Dynamics CRM on-premises support</a> focused on maintaining dependable operations. Practical activities may include reviewing configuration, investigating reported issues, checking integrations and data flows, assisting with administration tasks, and identifying changes that could improve maintainability. We distinguish this ongoing support from a new implementation: the priority is to understand the current environment, protect business continuity, and make controlled improvements as requirements evolve.</p>

            <h3>Customization, Integration, Security, and Performance</h3>
            <p>iFOX can help assess <a href="/dynamics-365-crm-services/Customization">CRM customizations</a> and <a href="/dynamics-365-crm-services/Integration">connected systems</a>, then plan changes that fit the existing solution. This may include reviewing forms, workflows, business rules, extensions, data exchanges, and integration dependencies. Security and performance work focuses on appropriate access controls, configuration review, process behavior, troubleshooting, and identifying bottlenecks or recurring issues. The goal is to support reliable users and data while keeping the environment easier to operate and change.</p>

            <h2>CRM Upgrade and Modernization Planning</h2>
            <p>CRM upgrade and modernization work begins with an assessment of the current environment, customizations, integrations, data, operational dependencies, and business priorities. iFOX can help organize upgrade considerations, identify areas that require testing or remediation, and sequence practical improvements. Modernization does not automatically mean moving to the cloud; an organization may first need to maintain and improve its on-premises environment based on its operational and technical requirements.</p>

            <h3>Migration Planning for Dynamics 365 Cloud</h3>
            <p>For organizations considering a move to Dynamics 365 cloud, iFOX can help separate <a href="/dynamics-365-crm-services/Migration">migration planning</a> from ongoing on-premises support. Planning may include reviewing data and customizations, documenting integrations, identifying process dependencies, considering target capabilities, and outlining validation and adoption activities. A cloud migration should be based on assessed requirements and readiness rather than treated as a replacement for maintaining the current environment. This distinction helps organizations make informed decisions while keeping existing CRM operations stable.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
